<title>HUNGARY: Hungary 7-yr govt bond price drops to 103.43 pct.</title>
<headline>Hungary 7-yr govt bond price drops to 103.43 pct.</headline>
<dateline>BUDAPEST 1997-01-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>The average price of Hungary's seven-year government bonds was set by auction at 103.43 percent of the face value, down from 103.64 percent at an auction on December 19, the Government Debt Management Agency said on Thursday.</p>
<p>BONDS OF THE82003/F SERIES</p>
<p>    Issue date		  October 17, 1996</p>
<p>    Total on offer  8	 5,000 million forints</p>
<p>  8 Total bids received     7,263 million forints</p>
<p>    Total allocated	   5,000 million forints</p>
<p>    Total issued		5,500 million forints @</p>
<p> 0  Minimum price	  0	  103.18 pct</p>
<p>    Average price	     0     103.43 pct</p>
<p>    Maximum price		     103.92 pct</p>
<p>NOTE - The bond bears a floating interest, calculated on March 20 and September 20 every year adding three percent to year-on-year consumer inflation. The interest is paid once a year, on September 24. The starting interest is 25.9 percent.</p>
<p>-- Budapest newsroom (36 1) 327 4040</p>
